 > Tip:
 >
-> Your app icon must be a png, and it should ideally have a resolution of 1024x1024px.
+> A PNG icon should ideally have a resolution of 1024x1024px.
+
+The SwiftPM packer also accepts an Icon Composer directory:
+
+```yaml
+iconPath: Resources/AppIcon.icon
+```
+
+This experimental path compiles SVG layers, groups, fills, and materials into
+`Assets.car` using AssetKit. It generates flat legacy PNGs and the matching
+Info.plist declarations. It requires `rsvg-convert` (`librsvg2-tools` on Linux,
+`brew install librsvg` on macOS). Keep the whole `.icon` directory, including
+`icon.json` and `Assets/`. Do not also add it to `resources`.
+
+Unsupported document fields cause a build error. See
+[AssetKit's supported subset and verification status](https://github.com/xtool-org/AssetKit/blob/main/docs/icon-composer.md).
+An existing top-level `Assets.car` conflicts with the generated catalog;
+catalog merging is not supported. The Xcode project generator currently does
+not support `iconPath`.
 
